There will be an anarchist forum in NYC this Thursday
(January 28) on the subject:

"Anarchism and Capitalism: Friends or Enemies"

Speakers: Perry Metzger (anarcho-capitalist) & Steve Shalom (anti-capitalist)

I'm sure many or most of you know Perry from the net; Steve is a professor 
of political science, writes for Z Magazine (among others), and is editor of
the book "Socialist Visions" (South End Press).  They will debate the
virtues of capitalism and its compatibility with anarchism.  (This won't be
a formal debate--the two will each get a chance to speak, and then there will
be a question-and-answer/discussion period open to everybody.)  This should
be a particularly lively forum.

This event is FREE (donations requested/appreciated)
Please come!

Place:
Penn South Community Center
369 Eighth Ave. (corner W. 29 St.)
NYC

Sponsor: Libertarian Book Club*


* The Libertarian Book Club is anarchist, not Libertarian.  The group
was founded in 1949 when the word "libertarian" meant "anarchist," and
refuses to change its name.




